WEBVTT

00:00:00.174 --> 00:00:03.164
What if every vehicle in India
turned electric overnight?

00:00:03.169 --> 00:00:04.619
At first, it sounds perfect.

00:00:04.750 --> 00:00:06.240
City air would get much cleaner,

00:00:06.610 --> 00:00:09.000
and India would use far less imported oil.

00:00:09.080 --> 00:00:10.310
But there's a big problem.

00:00:10.446 --> 00:00:13.956
Charging all those vehicles would
need huge amounts of electricity,

00:00:14.486 --> 00:00:16.896
and much of India's power
still comes from coal.

00:00:17.016 --> 00:00:19.042
There also wouldn't be enough chargers.

00:00:19.042 --> 00:00:20.412
Petrol pumps would close,

00:00:20.802 --> 00:00:24.292
and mechanics who only know petrol
engines would lose their jobs.

00:00:24.462 --> 00:00:28.332
The grid, the batteries, the jobs,
everything would have to change at once.

00:00:28.492 --> 00:00:32.213
Cleaner roads sound great, but where
would all that electricity come from?

00:00:32.213 --> 00:00:35.223
So what if every vehicle in
India went electric tomorrow?

